{"5168430":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"4:12 AM","steam_appid":5168430,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"dlc":[5214950],"detailed_description":"<strong>4:12 AM. That call has been ringing for twenty-seven years.<\/strong><br><br>December 20th, 1999. Ashwood, Pennsylvania — a half-empty town where a coal seam has burned underground since 1962. On the first night the county takes its overnight 911 desk back, the operator's chair belongs to Kate Morrow, who has spent six years unable to forget the one call she hung up on.<br><br>Twelve nights remain until the old switchboard shuts down on New Year's Eve. Pile-ups on snowed-in roads. CPR instructions that aren't getting through. A grandmother with dementia who calls every night. And every night at 4:12 AM, a call comes in from an address that no longer exists — in the voice of a girl who disappeared fifteen years ago.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Answer with your own voice<\/h2>Speak into your microphone and the caller listens — a local AI performs every character in real time. No dialogue trees: you listen, calm, press, and decide. Everything runs <strong>fully offline<\/strong>; your voice never leaves your machine.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Over 100 emergency calls<\/h2>37 story calls across twelve nights, plus a pool of 66 more — from life-or-death first-aid guidance to the small, strange troubles of a town at night. Every call can end differently depending on how you handle it.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Your judgment reshapes the town<\/h2>Fire, EMS, police — where do you send them, and how fast? Last night's decisions become tomorrow's headlines, change the calls that reach you, decide who survives, and branch into nine endings.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A dispatch room in 1999<\/h2>CRT monitors, paper call sheets, a handwritten notebook. In the last days before Y2K, the silence this town has kept across three decades — 1972, 1984, 1993 — begins to surface on the line.","about_the_game":"<strong>4:12 AM. That call has been ringing for twenty-seven years.<\/strong><br><br>December 20th, 1999. Ashwood, Pennsylvania — a half-empty town where a coal seam has burned underground since 1962. On the first night the county takes its overnight 911 desk back, the operator's chair belongs to Kate Morrow, who has spent six years unable to forget the one call she hung up on.<br><br>Twelve nights remain until the old switchboard shuts down on New Year's Eve. Pile-ups on snowed-in roads. CPR instructions that aren't getting through. A grandmother with dementia who calls every night. And every night at 4:12 AM, a call comes in from an address that no longer exists — in the voice of a girl who disappeared fifteen years ago.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Answer with your own voice<\/h2>Speak into your microphone and the caller listens — a local AI performs every character in real time. No dialogue trees: you listen, calm, press, and decide. Everything runs <strong>fully offline<\/strong>; your voice never leaves your machine.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Over 100 emergency calls<\/h2>37 story calls across twelve nights, plus a pool of 66 more — from life-or-death first-aid guidance to the small, strange troubles of a town at night. Every call can end differently depending on how you handle it.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Your judgment reshapes the town<\/h2>Fire, EMS, police — where do you send them, and how fast? Last night's decisions become tomorrow's headlines, change the calls that reach you, decide who survives, and branch into nine endings.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A dispatch room in 1999<\/h2>CRT monitors, paper call sheets, a handwritten notebook. In the last days before Y2K, the silence this town has kept across three decades — 1972, 1984, 1993 — begins to surface on the line.","short_description":"December 1999, the eve of Y2K. Twelve nights as the 911 operator of a dying Pennsylvania coal town. Speak with your own voice; a fully offline local AI plays every caller. Every night at 4:12 AM the phone rings: a girl missing for fifteen years. Who lives and who is lost depends on how you answer.","supported_languages":"Japanese, English, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Korean","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5168430\/59b3b0eb238392bc2f93471a8a5fa0ce8114b861\/header.jpg?t=1793753042","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5168430\/c69aa5df9c380a89dbc02a47c3bce0d9c9137233\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793753042","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5168430\/c69aa5df9c380a89dbc02a47c3bce0d9c9137233\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793753042","website":null,"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 10 64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> Quad-core CPU with AVX2 support<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 16 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> No GPU required (the AI runs on the CPU; replies are slower)<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 15 GB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Sound Card:<\/strong> Microphone optional (you can also play by typing)<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> A microphone is optional: answer calls by voice or by typing. All AI (dialogue and speech recognition) runs locally on your PC, no internet connection needed. Without a GPU with 10 GB+ VRAM, the AI runs on the CPU and replies take longer.<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 11<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> 8-core CPU<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 16 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> GPU with 10 GB+ VRAM (GeForce RTX 3080 \/ Radeon RX 6800 or better)<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 15 GB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Sound Card:<\/strong> Microphone (optional, for voice play)<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> Speaking into a microphone is recommended but optional; typing works too. All AI runs locally on your PC, no internet connection needed.<\/li><\/ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"developers":["Voreliq"],"publishers":["Voreliq"],"demos":[{"appid":5214950,"description":""}],"price_overview":{"currency":"USD","initial":1499,"final":1499,"discount_percent":0,"initial_formatted":"","final_formatted":"$14.99"},"packages":[1789091],"package_groups":[{"name":"default","title":"Buy 4:12 AM","description":"","selection_text":"Select a purchase option","save_text":"","display_type":0,"is_recurring_subscription":"false","subs":[{"packageid":1789091,"percent_savings_text":" ","percent_savings":0,"option_text":"4:12 AM - $14.99","option_description":"","can_get_free_license":"0","is_free_license":false,"price_in_cents_with_discount":1499}]}],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":false,"linux":false},"categories":[{"id":2,"description":"Single-player"},{"id":22,"description":"Steam Achievements"},{"id":62,"description":"Family Sharing"}],"genres":[{"id":"25","description":"Adventure"},{"id":"23","description":"Indie"},{"id":"28","description":"Simulation"}],"screenshots":[{"id":0,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5168430\/2839d53951bfb4a06b519a42c527efe4a853c1aa\/ss_2839d53951bfb4a06b519a42c527efe4a853c1aa.600x338.jpg?t=1793753042","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5168430\/2839d53951bfb4a06b519a42c527efe4a853c1aa\/ss_2839d53951bfb4a06b519a